From 711d14e824f0fc59985e30884f26b82eb50e600e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: josephrmoore <josephrmoore@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 06:17:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Extract events.log(), replace duplicate [module] print
 formatting

Every module hand-typed its own 'print(f"[modulename] message")' with
zero enforcement that the format stayed consistent. Centralized into
events.log(module_name, message) in events.py, which already owns
console+file logging for the event bus -- same responsibility,
different message type (ad-hoc diagnostics vs structured events).

Deliberately console-only, same as before -- does not also persist to
events.log, so this is a pure refactor, not a behavior change for
message delivery.

Incidental fixes riding along, flagged separately since they DO change
visible output slightly: config.py's three prints and db.py's
migration-applied print had no [module] prefix at all (the only ones
missing it) -- brought in line with the convention everything else
already followed.

Left alone deliberately: events.py's own event-line echo (structured
timestamp|event|payload format, not the ad-hoc diagnostic pattern),
_print_summary's block-report prints in ableton_scanner (deliberate
structured summary, not ad-hoc), and set_credential.py's prints
(interactive CLI text for a human running it directly, not module
diagnostic logging -- different kind, not a duplication).

Verified: py_compile on every touched file, full import-cycle check
across the whole chain (events/config/credentials/api_client/local_llm/
registry/router/db/file_utils/file_organizer/dedup_finder all import
cleanly), and functional regression against ableton_scanner's existing
fixture set -- identical output to before the refactor.
